{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 132, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, removing the edge 0->3 path leaves almost no route to the output, so accuracy collapses (pairs 14/18/22 vs 13/17/21)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, edge 5 is one of only two inputs to the output node, so deleting it hurts far more (79/80 vs 77/78)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 missing, the output relies on node 1 via edge 4, so cutting edge 0 removes nearly all conv computation (84 vs 83)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input->output path where none existed gives a much larger gain than swapping out an existing op (41 vs 42-44)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input->output edge restores a shortcut path, which helps much more than replacing a conv there (74 vs 73)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the input->output skip, an identity edge into the output restores residual-like gradient flow in a deep all-conv cell (90 vs 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip into the output compensates for a missing input->output shortcut, so it helps far more when edge 3 is none (92 vs 91)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 5 only carries useful signal if node 2 receives a strong input, which a conv on edge 1 provides (7 vs 8, 100 vs 99, 3 vs 2)."}, {"